# Focused gate: target/release/litex -strict -f examples/proof_nodes/atomic/by_builtin_rule/rounding_definition_bounds.lit
# Before: the following direct defining facts were rejected (see task journal).
# forall x R:
#     floor(x)<=x
#     x<floor(x)+1
#     ceil(x)-1<x
#     x<=ceil(x)
# Boundary: floor(0)<0 and ceil(0)>0 are false; floor(i) is outside the real domain.
# Now: the same direct facts pass without trust or a user theorem.

forall x R:
    floor(x)<=x
    x<floor(x)+1
    ceil(x)-1<x
    x<=ceil(x)
